lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3588:(`IsCleanBall` = the paper's *stickerball* = a shellable clean ball: it admits a clean shelling).
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3592:* **It is genuinely clean, including connected vertex links.**  `IsCleanBall M.support σ` provably
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3593:  entails `Clean3Complex M.support` via `IsCleanBall.clean3Complex` — exported here as the standalone
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3594:  endpoint `taut_clean3Complex`.  `Clean3Complex = Pure3 ∧ TriangleBounded3 ∧ Normal3` and
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3595:  `Normal3 = EdgeLinkConnected ∧ VertexLinkConnected`, so connected vertex links (dim-0 links) and
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3598:  `IsCleanShelling.clean3Complex`.
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3600:* **The proof actually establishes the stronger free-start statement.**  `IsCleanBall` asks only for
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3602:  clean shelling beginning with *any* prescribed tet (`FreelyCleanShellable`).  So the substance of
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3604:  induction; `theorem2_clean` simply forgets the head condition.  `IsCleanBall` (stickerball /
lean/Taut/Theorem3Clean.lean:3605:  shellable) and `FreelyCleanShellable` (free-start) are kept as *distinct* predicates on purpose —
